      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CARISSA'S BABY (2) put in a much better performance last start when in the placings at Launceston behind Raving Lunatic (29.97) in a Grade 5. Has the pace to be prominent. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings two times from three attempts. One of the contenders. ROMEO INDY (1) is worth forgiving last start after finishing fourth (26.11) from Box 3 at this track over 461m. Can measure up this time. FISHING YARI (8) returned a better run last time, finishing in the money (26.46) at this track behind Tapa Danior in a Grade 5. Has the early speed to land on the pace and can stick on. Form from her last run is proving strong. Expected to be in this for a long way. SCOOBY DANGER (7) is one of the chances after collecting a minor prize last time.",
